> File names every implementation must survive, one per line, UTF-8, no BOM.
> Read by abstraction-cas/python/test_abstraction_cas.py and by abstraction-cas/mixed.py, which puts the
> last one on CAS_PATH so Go, C++ and Python are all held to it. Blank lines and
> lines starting with > are skipped.
>
> Until 2026-09-09 no test in any of the three languages used a file name longer
> than one ASCII letter, and the Windows rename in Python had counted code points
> where the kernel counts UTF-16 units since it was written: one emoji in the name
> and the bytes landed under a name nobody asked for, while write returned.

